// The Supported mods tab (SupportedModList). Status: Works, Settings (works with Settings sync on), Partial or Broken.
// Write for players and hosts, one plain sentence per detail. Update this when a release changes what a mod gets.
{
  "general": [
    "Settings sync (players install ModderLords.Compat, which the launcher keeps up to date): the host's MCM settings reach every joining player, and live changes are sent at once. Players' own settings files are never touched.",
    "Per mod, the host chooses whether players get the server's settings or keep their own (Mods tab, since 1.5.0).",
    "Server, Client, Client-optional and Dependency-only roles per mod, and per-folder server/client exclusion, so art and UI stay off the headless server.",
    "Load order: dependencies are respected, Coop's position is shown, and mods that must load after Coop are moved for you or offered a Fix load order.",
    "Map-replacing mods: the server prepares its own copy of the map and handles missing home towns. Field battles avoid scenes that would crash.",
    "Kingdom votes of any mod's own types reach players, and players who do not vote in time are decided for by the AI.",
    "The game's \"inventory exchanged\" event fires in co-op, so delivery quests and mods that listen for it work.",
    "Experimental Server-only logic (Server tab, Advanced): a mod's campaign logic runs only on the host. Works for some mods only.",
    "The Mods tab shows a Works / Needs recipe / Broken / Unknown verdict per mod from the compatibility database, and you can submit your own findings."
  ],
